<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>At That Age Support</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Help, troubleshooting, and contact information for the At That Age iPhone app.">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#1f3a66">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/img/at-that-age-icon.png">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/img/at-that-age-icon.png">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/at-that-age.css">
  </head>
  <body class="support-page">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="/at-that-age/" aria-label="At That Age home">
        <img src="/img/at-that-age-icon.png" width="48" height="48" alt="">
        <span>At That Age</span>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="/at-that-age/">About the app</a>
        <a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="support-hero">
        <div class="support-shell">
          <p class="eyebrow">At That Age support</p>
          <h1>How can I help?</h1>
          <p>Find quick answers below, or send a support request if something isn’t working the way it should.</p>
          <a class="primary-link" href="#support-form">
            Contact support
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="support-content support-shell" id="troubleshooting">
        <div class="support-index" aria-label="On this page">
          <p class="eyebrow">Quick help</p>
          <a href="#photos">Photo access</a>
          <a href="#matches">Missing or incorrect matches</a>
          <a href="#faces">Teaching faces</a>
          <a href="#purchases">Purchases</a>
          <a href="#transfer">Moving to another iPhone</a>
        </div>

        <div class="support-answers">
          <article id="photos">
            <span class="support-icon" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
            <div>
              <h2>Photo access</h2>
              <p>At That Age needs access to your photo library to find pictures by date. Full access works best so photos aren’t missed.</p>
              <ol>
                <li>Open <strong>Settings</strong> on your iPhone.</li>
                <li>Choose <strong>Apps → At That Age → Photos</strong>.</li>
                <li>Select <strong>Full Access</strong>.</li>
              </ol>
              <p class="support-note">Your photos stay on your device. Photo search and face matching run locally on your iPhone.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article id="matches">
            <span class="support-icon" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
            <div>
              <h2>Missing or incorrect matches</h2>
              <p>The app searches around the exact target date, widening the window when needed. If a good photo is missing:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Confirm the child’s birthday in the Kids tab.</li>
                <li>Make sure At That Age has full photo access.</li>
                <li>Teach the app a few examples of that child’s face.</li>
                <li>Open another result and choose <strong>Use in side by side</strong>.</li>
              </ul>
              <p>If a photo shows the wrong child, tap <strong>Who’s this?</strong> and choose <strong>Neither</strong>. The app remembers that correction on your device.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article id="faces">
            <span class="support-icon" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
            <div>
              <h2>Teaching faces</h2>
              <p>Teaching faces is optional, but it improves matching—especially when siblings look alike.</p>
              <ol>
                <li>Open the <strong>Kids</strong> tab.</li>
                <li>Choose a child, then tap <strong>Teach face</strong>.</li>
                <li>Select that child in several photos sampled across their life and save.</li>
              </ol>
              <p>Face signatures never leave your device and are not sent to the app’s developer or any server.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article id="purchases">
            <span class="support-icon" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
            <div>
              <h2>Purchases and restoring access</h2>
              <p>Today’s comparison and one different comparison each day are free. Choosing any age or date is a one-time purchase—not a subscription.</p>
              <p>If you already purchased the unlock, open the Kids tab and tap <strong>Restore purchases</strong>. Make sure the iPhone is signed in to the same Apple Account used for the original purchase.</p>
              <p>Payments and entitlements are handled by Apple through the App Store.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article id="transfer">
            <span class="support-icon" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
            <div>
              <h2>Moving to another iPhone</h2>
              <p>A normal Quick Start or iCloud backup should carry your setup to a new iPhone automatically.</p>
              <p>For a fresh setup or a partner’s phone, open the Kids tab and choose <strong>Export settings</strong>. AirDrop the resulting <code>.atthatage</code> file or save it to Files, then open it on the other iPhone.</p>
              <p>The export contains kids, birthdays, and taught face signatures. It does not contain your photos.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="support-form-section support-shell" id="contact">
        <div class="support-form-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">Still need help?</p>
          <h2>Send a support request</h2>
          <p>Tell me what happened and I’ll follow up by email. Your iOS and app versions can help me investigate, but they’re optional.</p>
        </div>

        <form class="support-form" id="support-form" name="at-that-age-support" method="POST" data-netlify="true" data-netlify-honeypot="bot-field">
          <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="at-that-age-support">
          <input type="hidden" name="subject" data-remove-prefix value="New At That Age support request">
          <p class="form-honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
            <label>Leave this field empty <input name="bot-field" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label>
          </p>

          <div class="form-row">
            <label>
              Name
              <input type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" required>
            </label>
            <label>
              Email
              <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required>
            </label>
          </div>

          <label>
            What can I help with?
            <select name="topic" required>
              <option value="">Choose a topic</option>
              <option>Photo access</option>
              <option>Missing or incorrect matches</option>
              <option>Teaching faces</option>
              <option>Purchase or restore</option>
              <option>Backup or transfer</option>
              <option>Feedback or feature request</option>
              <option>Something else</option>
            </select>
          </label>

          <div class="form-row">
            <label>
              iOS version <span class="optional">Optional</span>
              <input type="text" name="ios-version" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="For example, 18.6">
            </label>
            <label>
              App version <span class="optional">Optional</span>
              <input type="text" name="app-version" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="Shown in the Kids tab">
            </label>
          </div>

          <label>
            What happened?
            <textarea name="message" rows="7" required placeholder="Describe what you expected and what happened instead."></textarea>
          </label>

          <div class="form-submit-row">
            <button type="submit">Send request <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
            <p>Only the information you enter here is sent. Your photos and app data are never attached.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="form-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </form>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <a class="brand footer-brand" href="/at-that-age/">
        <img src="/img/at-that-age-icon.png" width="36" height="36" alt="">
        <span>At That Age</span>
      </a>
      <p><a href="/at-that-age/">About the app</a> · <a href="#support-form">Contact support</a></p>
      <p>&copy; {{ page.date.getFullYear() }} Craig Sturgis</p>
    </footer>
    <script>
      (() => {
        const form = document.querySelector('#support-form');
        const status = form.querySelector('.form-status');
        const button = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');

        form.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
          event.preventDefault();
          if (!form.reportValidity()) return;

          button.disabled = true;
          button.textContent = 'Sending…';
          status.className = 'form-status';
          status.textContent = '';

          try {
            const response = await fetch('/', {
              method: 'POST',
              headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },
              body: new URLSearchParams(new FormData(form)).toString()
            });
            if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Submission failed');
            form.reset();
            status.className = 'form-status form-status-success';
            status.textContent = 'Your request was sent. I’ll reply to the email address you provided.';
          } catch (error) {
            status.className = 'form-status form-status-error';
            status.textContent = 'I couldn’t send that request. Please try again in a moment.';
          } finally {
            button.disabled = false;
            button.innerHTML = 'Send request <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>';
          }
        });
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
